Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL, NOT PACKAGED] ntdll: leave initial ARM64EC stack headroom

Base: The412Banner/proton-wine 256288853b206373cbf65b775143d33bb11035dd

An x64 startup injector can retain the suspended thread's RSP and redirect RIP
to a LoadLibraryW call. Native x64 starts below StackBase; the ARM64 path currently
starts at StackBase. The supplied Ubisoft stub then reaches the EC LoadLibraryW
entry with RSP = StackBase - 16 and writes to RSP + 32, outside the stack.

Reserve the x64 startup home space and return slot, rounded up to preserve ARM64
SP alignment. Keep native ARM64 and WOW64 startup unchanged. The offline replay
only verifies the failing x64 entry write; this candidate has NOT been built,
tested on Android, or applied by Aura's runtime packaging scripts.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
@@ -1532,6 +1532,11 @@ void init_syscall_frame( LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE entry, void *arg, BOOL suspend, TEB
     context.X18 = (DWORD64)teb;
     context.Sp  = (DWORD64)teb->Tib.StackBase;
     context.Pc  = (DWORD64)pRtlUserThreadStart;
-
+    /* Leave room for x64 startup code that redirects the initial PC without
+     * allocating its own home space. RtlUserThreadStart is a native ARM64
+     * entry here, so round the x64 0x28-byte reservation to 16-byte alignment.
+     */
+    if (is_arm64ec()) context.Sp -= 0x30;
+
     if ((i386_context = get_cpu_area( IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386 )))
     {
